sysinfo - any fact the kernel answers, by name

  sysinfo <key>          print one answer

The kernel describes itself through one interface, and every window and
tool reads from it; this prints the same answers raw. Useful keys:

  kernel cpu mem mem.hardware display display.adapter display.panel
  storage board bios uptime mounts svc clock threads irq apic mtrr
  quirks keymap font arch cmdline

A key the kernel does not know is refused rather than answered blankly.
